WEBVTT

NOTE Actual full-workspace tutorial recording. Prepared starter QA account; five later phases explicitly opened. No earned passes, AI, execution, edits or submissions. Normal speed; no added holds.

1
00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:06.560
1 of 6. Inspect the release configuration
Open Configuration to work through the pipeline and configuration files. Use the brief to understand what this isolated deployment exercise checks.

2
00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:12.760
2 of 6. Run the configuration selfcheck
Run selfcheck checks the saved configuration when its runner is available. It does not demonstrate Docker builds, CI execution, Compose startup or live HTTP health probes.

3
00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:18.640
3 of 6. Read the pipeline evidence
Open Pipeline for the actual check output. Use failures to revise the configuration. If the runner is unavailable, no successful execution can be claimed.

4
00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:24.680
4 of 6. Work through the incident drill
Open Incident drill to inspect its evidence, choose an investigation action and explain your response. The drill stays separate from a real deployment.

5
00:00:24.680 --> 00:00:31.080
5 of 6. Submit the saved release work
Submit the saved configuration and required evidence for review. Revisit specific feedback before resubmitting; only a valid passing review completes the phase.

6
00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:37.040
6 of 6. Return whenever you need help
Replay tutorial brings these steps back. Optional phase guide opens the lessons. In the workspace mentor, Guided offers hints. Agentic proposes changes: compare them, explain this exact version in your own words, then choose Apply only if your explanation is accepted. A changed proposal needs a new explanation.
